      <h3>Evidence before hype</h3>
      <p>Say what is known, what is still being studied and strengthen claims only when the evidence supports it.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Clear over complicated</h3>
      <p>Explain the practical point first. Give people the deeper science when they want it.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Useful first</h3>
      <p>Products, features and partnerships should solve a real problem, not exist just because they are marketable.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Keep improving</h3>
      <p>Change the formula, research or communication when better evidence and useful feedback point us there.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
